RS Chebyshev Ni(001) surface, calctype S, nsp=1 (collinear spin-polarised), LDA+U U=3 eV / J=0.7 eV on the d channel of types 1 (frozen Ni host), 3 (Ni-S) and 4 (Ni-S-1); no U on ES. hubbard_radial_moments='local', lld=200, 2500 channels, fixed E_F -0.076743, beta 0.005 Broyden, ldm_beta 0.3. Same geometry and recursion settings as ni001_u0.

Files: input.nml (surface); bulk_input.nml (Ni bulk host); Ni.nml + Ni_dm.nml (U=3/J=0.7 bulk host, frozen in the surface run; Ni_dm.nml sha256 aad75ab2... is the one recorded in Ni.nml); ES.nml, Ni-S.nml, Ni-S-1.nml (seeds, copied from ni001_u0, the converged U=0 surface).

Recipe:
1. Host: bulk_input.nml run in a directory holding the U=0 Ni.nml from ni001_u0 (chebyshev, nsp=1, lld=200, 2500 channels, rc=100, beta 0.05, ldm_beta 0.3, conv_thr 1e-8). 31 steps in the first part, restarted once from Ni_scf.nml after the job was killed by a pkill of mine (restart also needed Ni_dm.nml next to it). Converged, Diff 8.9e-9. ql window over the last 12 snapshots: d_up 9.93e-09, d_dn 2.53e-08, moment 1.22e-08. Stored Hubbard values 0.2205/0.05145 Ry. Host: moment 0.766353 muB (>0.4), n_d 8.590988, E_F (free) -0.076743 Ry, etot -3037.6067720042438 Ry.
2. Energy window: d-PDOS at the window edges 0 to 1e-5 states/Ry against peaks of 32-50 (nearly converged U=3 host and the U=0 surface); the >1%-of-peak d band is about -0.47 to 0.84 Ry inside -0.92 to 1.59 Ry (E_F-shifted).
3. Surface: input.nml run in a directory holding the seeds, Ni.nml and Ni_dm.nml. 3 MPI ranks x 2 OpenMP threads, Release build, ~70 s/step. Guard (6c69dcd4) did not fire (HUBBARD_RUN provenance=PASS, energy_routing=off).

Convergence. The run was launched with conv_thr 1.0e-7 and ran all 200 steps. On the user's instruction conv_thr in input.nml was then raised to 5.0e-6 and the run taken as converged. Nothing was rerun with 5.0e-6. Diff per step: 1: 1.17e-1; 6: 1.37e-1 (peak); 17: 8.7e-3; 49: 3.0e-3; 100: 8.5e-4; 127: 4.6e-4; 150: 1.1e-5; 179: 4.963e-6 (first below 5e-6); 200: 3.501e-6. Diff exceeds 5e-6 again at steps 182 and 196 (max after step 179: 6.01e-6).
