Deepest layer (Ni-S-1) minus host: U=3 moment -0.052950 muB (step 200), n_d +0.044810; U=0 moment -0.034174 muB, n_d +0.041001.

Observations, not diagnosed: the early steps overshoot (steps 2-5 n_d ~9.4 on the surface layers, Diff spikes at steps 6, 9, 12) before settling; the surface run rewrote the frozen host's Ni_dm.nml (only the header line iteration = 31 became 200; sha256 now b614e9be...).

U->0 wiring evidence (reduced deck: nstep 1, lld 50, 500 channels, U on d of Ni, Ni-S, Ni-S-1, J=0, against the same deck without U): etot shift of Ni-S 1.99e-7, 1.89e-6, 1.88e-5 Ry at U = 1e-4, 1e-3, 1e-2 eV (ratios 9.53, 9.95 per decade). Wiring evidence only.
